      "english": "he was the Archon of the city.",
      "source": "The Life of John the Kalybites part 1",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:lives.john_kalybites.budge:1-45",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲛⲑⲟϥ ⲇⲉ ⲙⲡⲉ**ϥ**ⲧⲁⲙⲟϥ ϫⲉⲛⲛⲉϥϭⲓⲥⲓ ⲛϩⲏⲧ .",
      "english": "As for him, he did not let him know it, lest he should become proud of heart.",
      "source": "Life of Isaac of Alexandria - part 1",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:lives.boh_isaac.amelineau_ed:1-19",
      "dialect": "bohairic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲛⲧⲟϥ ⲇⲉ ⲡⲉϫⲁϥ ⲛⲁⲓ ϫⲉⲟⲛⲛⲟⲫⲣⲓⲟⲥ ⲡⲉ ⲡⲁⲣⲁⲛ · ⲁⲩⲱ ⲉⲓⲥ ⲥⲉ ⲛⲣⲟⲙⲡⲉ ϯϣⲟⲟⲡ ϩⲛϯⲉⲣⲏⲙⲓⲁ · ⲉⲓⲙⲟⲟϣⲉ ϩⲛⲛⲧⲟⲟⲩ ⲛⲧϩⲉ ⲛⲛⲉⲑⲏⲣⲓⲟⲛ · ⲁⲩⲱ ⲙⲡⲓⲛⲁⲩ ⲉⲣⲱⲙⲉ ⲉⲓⲥⲟⲟⲩⲛ ⲙⲙⲟ**ϥ** ·",
      "english": "And he said unto me, 'Onnophrios is my name. And behold, I have lived in this desert for sixty years. I wander about in the mountains like the wild animals, and I never see any man who recognizeth me.",
      "source": "Life of Onnophrius part 1",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:lives.onnophrius.budge:1-9",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲫⲏ ⲉⲧⲉⲡⲉϥϩⲱⲃ ⲛⲁⲣⲱⲕϩ ϥⲛⲁϯⲟⲥⲓ ⲛⲑⲟϥ ⲇⲉ **ϥ**ⲛⲁⲛⲟϩⲉⲙ ⲡⲁⲓⲣⲏϯ ⲇⲉ ϩⲱⲥ ⲉⲃⲟⲗ ϩⲓⲧⲉⲛⲟⲩⲭⲣⲱⲙ .",
      "english": "If any man's work is burned, he will suffer loss, but he himself will be saved, but as through fire.",
      "source": "Bohairic 1 Corinthians 3 (Digital Edition)",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:nt.1cor.bohairic_ed:3",
      "dialect": "bohairic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲛⲧⲟϥ ⲙⲉⲛ ⲙⲡⲟⲩϩⲉ ⲉⲣⲟϥ · ⲁⲗⲗⲁ ⲁⲩϩⲉ ⲉⲡⲉϥⲥⲁⲛⲇⲁⲗⲓⲟⲛ · ⲙⲛⲟⲩⲕⲁϩ ⲛⲃⲣⲣⲉ ϩⲣⲁⲓ ϩⲙⲡⲙⲁ ⲛⲧⲁ**ϥ**ⲃⲱⲕ ⲉⲡⲉⲥⲏⲧ ⲉⲣⲟϥ ·",
      "english": "and they could not find him, but they found his sandal, and the newly-dug ground in the place where he had gone down into the earth.",
      "source": "Dormition of John MERC.AD in Budge ed.",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:misc.dormition_john.budge",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    }
